TDC 11/20/14
AVI PROFESSIONAL CORPORATION    1103 Old Town Lane; Suite 101, Cheyenne, WY 82009 phone: 307.637.6017
Page 1 of 5
CHANGE ORDER NO. One

November 19, 2014

CITY OF CHEYENNE CONTRACT NO: 6137

ENGINEER'S PROJECT NO: 3425.12

PROJECT:
Polk Avenue Greenway

CONTRACTOR: Reiman Corporation

CONTRACT FOR: Roadway and Greenway construction on Polk Avenue from U.S. 30 to East
Pershing Blvd.

TO:
Mr. Rich Bolkovatz, Project Manager, Reiman Corporation and Subsidiary

CONTRACTOR

You are directed to make the changes noted below in the subject Contract:

Nature of the Changes

Subgrade Stabilization:  Based on the underground conditions found during the installation of
the storm sewer from 7+44 to 11+50 and proof roll from Sta. 1+00 to 4+50 , the subgrade area
is comprised of lenses of silty sands, clayey sands, and organic and silty clays.  Stability of the
subgrade for the future roadway and Greenway was very sensitive to moisture and the depth
and location of the lenses of organic material.  Therefore, stabilization of the subgrade will be
required to support the future surfacing material and curb and gutter.  Two types of remediation
will be required:

1) Fly Ash Stabilization from Sta. 1+00 to 4+50± (i.e. 28’ from TBC to TBC):
Treat the pavement subgrade by tilling the existing material with the addition of a
mixture of Class C fly ash mixing, shaping, and compaction of the mixed material
to the required density in conformity with the typical sections, lines, and grades
as shown on the plans.  Additional mobilization will be required for additional sub-
contractor.

2) Sub-excavation and placement of import structural backfill from Sta. 6+85 to Sta. 4+50,
7+44 to Sta. 11+00, (i.e. 28’ to 34.5’ top back of curb to top back of curb and Sub-
excavate 18” below bottom of crushed base.

Sub-excavate 18” of unsuitable material from bottom of proposed surfacing and
dispose of at a site determined by the Contractor
```

