
Install 5” of Crushed Base Special under the 2’ wide Curb and Gutter Type ‘A’.

3) Sub-excavation and placement of import structural backfill Sta. 6+85 to 10+50 Greenway
(i.e. 10’ wide).

Sub-excavate 12” of unsuitable material from bottom of proposed surfacing and
dispose of at a site determined by the Contractor

Install reinforced biaxial Mirafi Geogrid per the manufacturers recommendations

Install 12” of structural backfill using crushed concrete

Unanticipated Field Conditions:

Relocate Watermain:  During pipe trench excavation on main storm line at the intersection of
Cheyenne Street and Polk Avenue, an existing waterline was found to be closer in proximity the
proposed 8’ diameter manhole (A-5) than anticipated.  Relocation of the water main was
required to meet WYDEQ/ BOPU requirements.  Additional 8” DR-14 PVC watermain, (2) 8” 45°
bends, and Megalug mechanical joint restraints for PVC pipe were required to complete the
relocation of the watermain.

Unsuitable Material:  During the grading of the northwest side of the project, a mixture of
asphalt and trash were encountered within the right-of-way.  This material was planned for as
unclassified excavation however, the nature of the material required removal and proper
disposal offsite which was not anticipated.

Additional Mobilization:  Due to adverse weather days, delay in relocation of dry utilities by
Cheyenne Light, Fuel, and Power, and additional work on the project, additional time will be
required to complete the project. Additionally, project sequencing was altered due to delays in
the project which have impacted workloads of the Contractor and Sub-contractors.  This
alteration required additional days for completion of the project.

In addition, maintenance of the structural erosion control features and traffic control were
required due to the increased time of the project.

Dry Utility Relocation Delay:  The construction documents outlined that a third party (i.e.
Cheyenne Light, Fuel, and Power) would relocate gas main, gas services, and (4) four electrical
power poles prior to construction beginning on Polk Avenue project.  Due to unforeseen
circumstances, the dry utilities were not able to be relocated and an additional gas line was
installed on the south portion of the project.  These changes impacted the efficiency,
sequencing, and schedule for an unreasonable amount of time. As a result, additional
mobilization was required to complete the project.
```

